Z||000001||mrfixit58||01-26-2001||04:05 PM||||Do a search on the topic. This topic was discussed in great detail some time ago. Unfortunatly, the consensus was by the time you spend the time and money to install a turbo, you'd be better off exchanging the whole motor for a v-6 or better. For something really neat, look at this thread, installing a 4.9 Caddy motor in place of the Duke:<BR> <A HREF="http://sites.netscape.net/bubbajoexx/homepage" TARGET=_blank>http://sites.netscape.net/bubbajoexx/homepage</A> <P>Heck, I want to pull my v-6 to do this.<P>Welcome to the forum,<BR>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>||||reg||4
